    skos:prefLabel 'atmosphere_moles_of_carbon_monoxide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The construction "atmosphere_moles_of_X" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula of carbon monoxide is CO.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12S3'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S30/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S30/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S30/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T16:21:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called "molarity", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \'nitrogen\' or a phrase such as \'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\'. The phrase \'expressed_as\' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12S30'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T16:21:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called "molarity", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \'nitrogen\' or a phrase such as \'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\'. The phrase \'expressed_as\' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12S31'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S51/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S51/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S51/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T16:21:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_atmosphere_moles_of_methyl_bromide'@en ;
    skos:definition '"tendency_of_X" means derivative of X with respect to time.  The construction "atmosphere_moles_of_X" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for methyl bromide is CH3Br. The IUPAC name for methyl bromide is bromomethane.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12S51'^^xsd:string .
