    skos:prefLabel 'atmosphere_moles_of_peroxynitric_acid'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The construction "atmosphere_moles_of_X" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for peroxynitric acid, sometimes referred to as PNA, is HO2NO2.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N173'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N174/1/> .
