    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_hexachlorobiphenyl_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \'nitrogen\' or a phrase such as \'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\'. The chemical formula for hexachlorobiphenyl is C12H4Cl6.  This structure of this species consists of two linked benzene rings, each of which is additionally bonded to three chlorine atoms.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N269'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N270/1/> .
