    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \'nitrogen\' or a phrase such as \'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\'. The phrase \'expressed_as\' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N302'^^xsd:string .
