    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'atmosphere_mass_content_of_ethane'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The "atmosphere content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for ethane is C2H6. Ethane is a member of the group of hydrocarbons known as alkanes.  There are standard names for the alkane group as well as for some of the individual species.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N40'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N41/1/> .
