    skos:prefLabel 'mole_concentration_of_propene_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called "molarity", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \'nitrogen\' or a phrase such as \'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\'. The chemical formula for propene is C3H6. Propene is a member of the group of hydrocarbons known as alkenes.  There are standard names for the alkene group as well as for some of the individual species.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N504'^^xsd:string .
