    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_tracer_xy_laplacian_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Diffusivity is also sometimes known as the coefficient of diffusion. Diffusion occurs as a result of a gradient in the spatial distribution of mass concentration, temperature or momentum.  The diffusivity may be very different in the vertical and horizontal directions. "xy diffusivity" means the lateral along_coordinate component of diffusivity due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.  xy diffusivities are used in some ocean models to counteract the numerical instabilities inherent in certain implementations of rotated neutral diffusion. "laplacian diffusivity" means diffusivity for use with a Laplacian diffusion operator.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N566'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N574/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N574/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N574/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'radiation_frequency'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Frequency is the number of oscillations of a wave per unit time.  The radiation frequency can refer to any electromagnetic wave, such as light, heat radiation and radio waves.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N574'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N577/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N577/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N577/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'reference_sea_water_density_for_boussinesq_approximation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea water density is the in-situ density (not the potential density). For a rigid lid Boussinesq geopotential ocean model the density of the sea water is maintained at a constant reference density.  In a model using the rigid lid Boussinesq approximation , the vertical grid coordinates (and hence the grid cell volumes) are time invariant.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N577'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N579/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N579/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N579/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_density'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea surface density is the density of sea water near the surface (including the part under sea-ice, if any).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N579'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N580/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N580/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N580/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_age_since_surface_contact'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Sea water age since surface contact" means the length of time elapsed since the sea water in a grid cell was last in the surface level of an ocean model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N580'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N581/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N581/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N581/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_mass'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name "sea_water_mass" is the total mass of liquid seawater in the global oceans, including enclosed seas.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N581'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N582/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N582/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N582/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_mass_per_unit_area'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea_water_mass_per_unit_area is the mass per unit area of the sea water contained within each grid cell.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N582'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N583/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N583/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N583/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_pressure_at_sea_floor'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Sea water pressure" is the pressure that exists in the medium of sea water.  It includes the pressure due to overlying sea water, sea ice, air and any other medium that may be present.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N583'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N585/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N585/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N585/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_volume'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name "sea_water_volume" is the total volume of liquid seawater in the global oceans, including enclosed seas.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N585'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N589/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N589/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N589/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'square_of_upward_ocean_mass_transport'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  Ocean transport means transport by all processes, both sea water and sea ice.  "square_of_X" means X*X.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N589'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N590/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N590/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N590/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'stratiform_cloud_longwave_emissivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Emissivity is the ratio of the power emitted by an object to the power that would be emitted by a perfect black body having the same temperature as the object. The emissivity is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength or radiation_frequency is included to specify either the wavelength or frequency. In an atmosphere model, stratiform cloud is that produced by large-scale convergence (not the convection schemes).  "longwave" means longwave radiation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N590'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N591/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N591/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N591/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sunlit_binary_mask'@en ;
    skos:definition 'X_binary_mask has 1 where condition X is met, 0 elsewhere.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N591'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N594/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N594/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N594/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_longwave_emissivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Emissivity is the ratio of the power emitted by an object to the power that would be emitted by a perfect black body having the same temperature as the object. The emissivity is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength or radiation_frequency is included to specify either the wavelength or frequency. The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere.  "longwave" means longwave radiation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N594'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N595/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N595/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N595/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_microwave_emissivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Emissivity is the ratio of the power emitted by an object to the power that would be emitted by a perfect black body having the same temperature as the object. The emissivity is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength or radiation_frequency is included to specify either the wavelength or frequency. The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N595'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N596/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N596/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N596/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'temperature_flux_due_to_evaporation_expressed_as_heat_flux_out_of_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Evaporation is the conversion of liquid or solid into vapor.  (The conversion of solid alone into vapor is called "sublimation".)  The quantity with standard name temperature_flux_due_to_evaporation_expressed_as_heat_flux_out_of_sea_water is the heat energy carried by the transfer of water away from the liquid ocean through the process of evaporation.  It is distinct from the transfer of latent heat and is calculated relative to the heat that would be transported by water evaporating at zero degrees Celsius. It is calculated as the product QevapCpTevap, where Qevap is the mass flux of evaporating water (kg m-2 s-1), Cp is the specific heat capacity of water and Tevap is the temperature in degrees Celsius of the evaporating water. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N596'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N597/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N597/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N597/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'temperature_flux_due_to_rainfall_expressed_as_heat_flux_into_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name temperature_flux_due_to_rainfall_expressed_as_heat_flux_into_sea_water is the heat energy carried by rainfall entering the sea at the sea surface.  It is calculated relative to the heat that would be carried by rainfall entering the sea at zero degrees Celsius.  It is calculated as the product QrainCpTrain, where Qrain is the mass flux of rainfall entering the sea (kg m-2 s-1), Cp is the specific heat capacity of water and Train is the temperature in degrees Celsius of the rain water entering the sea surface. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N597'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N599/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N599/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N599/>;
    dc:modified '2009-07-06T15:41:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_acetic_acid_due_to_dry_deposition'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The "atmosphere content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.  "tendency_of_X" means derivative of X with respect to time.  "Dry deposition" is the sum of turbulent deposition and gravitational settling. The chemical formula for acetic_acid is CH3COOH. The IUPAC name for acetic acid is ethanoic acid.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N599'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N6/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N6/1/>
