    skos:prefLabel 'atmosphere_mass_content_of_propane'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The "atmosphere content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for propane is C3H8. Propane is a member of the group of hydrocarbons known as alkanes.  There are standard names for the alkane group as well as for some of the individual species.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N96'^^xsd:string .
